{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the probability of obtaining a favorable outcome, treating outcome differences as negligible. Here, both lotteries offer a positive monetary outcome (4000 in A, 3000 in B) with non-zero probability and 0 otherwise. The favorable outcome is any positive gain. The probability of a favorable outcome is 20% for Lottery A and 25% for Lottery B. Since the reason considers the outcome amounts (4000 vs 3000) as negligible, the comparison reduces to choosing the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, which is Lottery B (25% > 20%). Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery B.",
